 "result_text": "The issue asks for new unit tests, but you told me to change source only, so I added no tests. Instead I fixed three bugs in the source that sit in the uncovered code. The existing 17 tests pass. I didn't re-run the coverage report, so I can't say how much the numbers moved.\n\n- **`tes/models.py`, `Task.is_valid`:** The check on `env` and `tags` looped over the dict directly, which yields only keys, so `for k, v in ...` would fail on any non-empty dict. It now uses `.items()`. The type check also tested `k` twice and never `v`. It now checks that both key and value are strings.\n- **`tes/client.py`, `wait`:** The timeout message was missing its `f` prefix, so it printed the literal text `{response.as_dict()}`. It is now an f-string.\n\nI didn't change `tes/utils.py` or the remaining uncovered lines in `client.py` and `models.py`. The test-only coverage gaps are still open.",
